  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_3369f40c8d314d63a420a5470f5510e6",
      "statement": "Every data-channel message is a protobuf Message (ts-proto-generated from src/proto/message.proto) carrying a file id plus exactly one payload: metaData, chunk, or receiveEvent (ACCEPT/REJECT/RECEIVED_CHUNK/VALIDATE_ERROR).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://package.json#L14-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c770b505f1052aced7b5390d52620c6c823d1d26889b5a183370fb23b46348b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/proto/message.proto#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f8c0ab1d2ddf1af4c03d3743789407e5f7307442c33e3dfe52c728531974356:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d169d7f279a84b80aefc309c6ab36c09",
      "statement": "File ids are crypto.randomUUID() values rather than filenames, so same-named files in one session keep distinct ids and their chunks never cross-wire; metaData.name is used for display only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/sender/Sender.svelte#L202-L213",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5119ef49a552fde66bb040242a0d38801417b7426d7cbc99165cba4f7c64ea87:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0489f3cde91743e7b351af897e8841ab",
      "statement": "The sender maintains per-file state in a reactive map with lifecycle Pending -> WaitingAccept -> Processing -> Success; on ACCEPT it starts the chunk loop, on REJECT or VALIDATE_ERROR it records the error and resets the file to Pending (retryable).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/sender/Sender.svelte#L46-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3a38db575ead4a8e155b569fb21fd2b1b4bb03b75e167d1f6300130da961b0b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/type.ts#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:91a5537e90fc962018cc021cbc2a7ff1c1abc74c3803bcc31d39ab33003b9c9f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fa837c572a3542b392cf3d6ec0f34834",
      "statement": "The transfer protocol is receiver-ack chunking: the receiver enqueues each incoming chunk onto a per-file serialized chain (onChunkData), and processChunk sends EVENT_RECEIVED_CHUNK at the start of each task, so the sender sends at most one next chunk per ack until offset reaches metaData.size — backpressure pacing the transfer with the sender one round-trip ahead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/receiver/Receiver.svelte#L119-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:02b3f1df535970c554616e3e3b67562305f1c18643a11f5b377240e17a725827:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/sender/Sender.svelte#L54-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eaadcb71c57d02039c5a0546c72b3589959f7b905cd799748a7410545a338b27:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6db6ca55760d4a5dbdf53c81700b8f96",
      "statement": "A defensive empty-chunk guard aborts the send with an 'Invalid chunk size' error when a chunk reads 0 bytes while bytes remain, preventing an infinite loop of empty sends caused by an invalid chunkSize (e.g. a crafted 'c' URL param).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/sender/Sender.svelte#L109-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:812cf14172a7ce32f44385f18a5e45a68666d89ffa9c9ec8d5344b0e646debee:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_390ca4161cab44d1a713439e1d4b2172",
      "statement": "Progress and bitrate UI updates are throttled by PROGRESS_UPDATE_UI_STEP (3 percentage points) using non-reactive stats mirrors, and pause/resume is implemented via a per-file stop flag where onContinue re-emits a synthetic RECEIVED_CHUNK event to restart the chunk loop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/sender/Sender.svelte#L127-L141",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c18d2b572062cc144d46f9c38c1ae8d0fbf8364d8eadb9b76c82fd155b153d64:"
